mission "A Convenient Forgery"
    name "A Convenient Forgery"
    description "Confront the broker selling false royal instruments and learn who paid him."
    source "Wreckers' Moon"
    destination "Gallows Key"
    reward 1005
    speaker offer "Silas Rook"
    speaker visit "Silas Rook"
    speaker complete "Silas Rook"
    to offer
        has "The Sound Beneath the Soundings: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Silas Rook has spread brass instruments across his counter. Their royal stamps look convincing at a glance, but the graduations do not match from one instrument to the next.`
            `Rook lifts one of the instruments and turns it in his hand. "A broker is selling these as genuine royal survey tools. They are not. I want to know who paid for the forgery before he slips out of the islands."`
            choice
                `"You can count on my ship. What is the first step?"`
                    accept
                `"Before I agree, tell me what I might be sailing into."`
                    goto details
                `"My crew did not sign on for this kind of trouble."`
                    close
            label details
                `He taps the false stamp with a fingernail. "Men do not counterfeit a crown's seal for pocket money. Someone wants these instruments trusted by captains who do not know any better. Find out who placed the order."`
                choice
                    `"I will do what I can. We should get underway."`
                        accept
                    `"That risk is not mine to take."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted A Convenient Forgery. Confront the broker selling false royal instruments and learn who paid him."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Gallows Key, Silas examines the broker's marks beside the recovered records. He finds the same private seal on the order. "These instruments were made to give false authority to a false chart," he says. "Someone is paying to make the old expedition's trail look official."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Rook wraps one of the instruments in cloth. "That is enough to follow the money. A forgery is useful only while somebody believes it. We have put a crack in that belief—and found the hand behind it."`
        log "Completed A Convenient Forgery. Received 1005 gold. Confront the broker selling false royal instruments and learn who paid him."
